{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && cat > update-10.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The sealed-partition experiment was executed and retained (CheckRun f66fa4e4e0514f7e95b7788032144a30, exit 0, outcome tests_passed). With the harness fixed so that the partner really is isolated from the majority, a legal five-node history both reaches the snapshot-boundary precondition and leaves the peer unrepairable: it installs the same snapshot ~668 times in the ~1.5 s window while its applied index stays pinned at the snapshot index and its advertised last index stays above it. This update records the measured interpretation, promotes the observed operands to a Fact, and withdraws the earlier negative reading of this history.\\\",\n  \\\"sources\\\": [\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-repl10\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"replication.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 220, \\\"end_line\\\": 300, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-repl-snap10\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"replication.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 299, \\\"end_line\\\": 375, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-installsnap10\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"raft.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 1814, \\\"end_line\\\": 1953, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-lastindex10\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"state.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 157, \\\"end_line\\\": 174, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-compact10\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"snapshot.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 216, \\\"end_line\\\": 262, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" }\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@b-sealed-partition-witness\\\",\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"fact\\\",\n      \\\"statement\\\": \\\"Executed five-node witness. divergent_prefix: base_index 2, divergence_index 3, partitioned_leader_last_index 7, partner_last_index 7, partner_store 1..7, partner_replicated_uncommitted true. successor_snapshot: snapshot_index 4, snapshot_term 3, old_leader_term 2, successor_last_index 4, successor_store_first/last 0 (fully compacted). Timeline after the heal at 0/200/400/700/1000/1300 ms: partner InstallSnapshot count 96, 205, 314, 425, 542, 658 while partner_applied_index stayed 4, partner_last_index stayed 7, the partner's store held only 5..7 with entry 5 at term 2 (entries 3,4 absent), the two other majority followers held entries 3,4 at term 3, and the successor's store stayed empty. rejoin_observe: restores_before 0, restores_early 658, restores_late 668, partner_applied_index 4, partner_last_index 7, partner_store 5..7, successor_applied_index 4, successor_commit_index 4.\\\",\n      \\\"conditions\\\": \\\"One process, root package '.', MakeClusterCustom with five bootstrapped nodes over InmemTransport and InmemStore (FileSnapshotStore per node), TrailingLogs=0, HeartbeatTimeout=ElectionTimeout=LeaderLeaseTimeout=1s; the fault is a two-sided partition of {leader, partner} from the other three peers, healed with FullyConnect after the successor snapshotted inside the partner's stale suffix. Frozen snapshot fd2d6988362c434e9fda87b87c5fb0df.\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-repl10\\\", \\\"src-repl-snap10\\\", \\\"src-installsnap10\\\", \\\"src-lastindex10\\\", \\\"src-compact10\\\"],\n      \\\"executions\\\": { \\\"f66fa4e4e0514f7e95b7788032144a30\\\": [1, 2, 3, 8, 9] }\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"interpretations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"b836c3a8cfc549188ebed6183f15f019-question-0\\\",\n      \\\"experiment_id\\\": \\\"b836c3a8cfc549188ebed6183f15f019-experiment\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-repl10\\\", \\\"src-repl-snap10\\\", \\\"src-installsnap10\\\", \\\"src-lastindex10\\\", \\\"src-compact10\\\"],\n      \\\"executions\\\": { \\\"f66fa4e4e0514f7e95b7788032144a30\\\": [1, 2, 9] },\n      \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"violated\\\",\n      \\\"defect_claim\\\": \\\"asserted\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The predicate under test was that a follower which rejoins with an earlier-term entry at the current leader's snapshot index either converges or is repaired by one snapshot. Retained receipt CheckRun f66fa4e4e0514f7e95b7788032144a30 contradicts it, so the comparison is violated. Applicability is established by observed producers, not by construction: index 1 shows the precondition arose from the partitioned leader's own AppendEntries (partner_last_index 7, partner_store 1..7, partner_replicated_uncommitted true), and index 2 shows the successor's snapshot at index 4 with its store fully compacted (first/last 0). Index 9 then shows 668 InstallSnapshot installs on the partner over the ~1.5 s window with restores_before 0, while partner_applied_index stayed 4 (the snapshot index), partner_last_index stayed 7, and its store held only 5..7 with 3,4 absent; the timeline at indices 3-8 shows the count rising monotonically (96, 205, 314, 425, 542, 658) with no change in applied or last index. Mechanism, consistent with the source: the partner's last-entry view still names index 7 (or 5..7) at the earlier term while the leader's boundary entry is at index 4 and term 3, so the boundary append is rejected; the leader rewinds nextIndex to 4; setPreviousLog(4) needs the leader's entry 3, which compaction removed, so setupAppendEntries returns ErrLogNotFound and replicateTo branches to SEND_SNAP; sendLatestSnapshot re-installs the same snapshot and resets nextIndex to 5, restoring the same rejection on the next attempt. No enclosing protection was observed: the peer kept installing the snapshot for the whole window, its applied index and advertised last index never moved, and the two other majority followers, which do hold the correct entries 3,4, are not consulted. Bounded-liveness statement from this receipt: after a legal trigger (a leader whose log was compacted to its snapshot index plus a peer that had received uncommitted entries from the previous leader and is then isolated and rejoined) the peer makes no progress for the observed ~1.5 s interval and the leader repeats whole-snapshot transfers at roughly 100-200 per 200 ms with no enabled repair under those conditions. This also resolves the reachability question affirmatively and retires the earlier negative result: the previous harness had left the partner<->majority links open, so the partner had already been repaired before its heal; sealing the partition is what exposes the defect.\\\",\n      \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n        \\\"The superseded negative result (restores 0 and partner store 1..4 with the successor's store empty) is not counterevidence any more: it was produced by an incomplete partition that let the successor repair the partner during the partition. Its cause is explained, and it is retained as a superseded harness result.\\\",\n        \\\"Only one configuration was executed (five nodes, TrailingLogs=0, equal 1 s timeouts, in-process transports); the assertion is scoped to those conditions and the stated fault, not to all clusters.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"limitations\\\": [\n        \\\"The snapshot transfers are counted through the follower FSM's Restore count rather than by instrumenting the wire, so the number identifies installs of the same snapshot, not identical RPC bytes.\\\",\n        \\\"The observation interval is ~1.5 s; non-progress is asserted for that interval with the mechanism above, not as a proof of infinite stalling.\\\",\n        \\\"Behaviour with default TrailingLogs (where a leader retains entries below its snapshot index) was not sampled; the executed basis is a leader compacted to its snapshot boundary.\\\",\n        \\\"One process and one peer under test; no external faults beyond the partition and heal.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"joint_history\\\": \\\"Single receipt: all three cited indices come from one execution of the registered experiment on the same frozen snapshot, and the two observations associate the same partner across the same partition/heal history (index 1 establishes the precondition and identifies the partner, index 2 the successor's compaction, index 9 the post-heal interval).\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\nJSON\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update-10.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
