{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"Clean control: with `TrailingLogs=3` the same history converges (0 snapshots); with 0 it loops. Shipping this."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cp /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft/tmp/w3/assurance_generated_test.go /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft/assurance_generated_test.go && cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && cat > update-11.json <<'JSON'\n{\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Added a competing-cause control for the now-asserted snapshot-boundary loop. The sealed-partition harness runs the same legal five-node history twice, differing only in how much of its log the successor leader keeps when it snapshots inside the follower's stale suffix: with TrailingLogs=0 the leader's retained log begins above the index the follower's prev-log check needs and the loop occurs; with TrailingLogs=3 the leader keeps the entries below the boundary and the same history converges with no snapshot at all. The control is registered so the controller retains the receipt.\\\",\n  \\\"sources\\\": [\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-compact11\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"snapshot.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 216, \\\"end_line\\\": 262, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-repl11\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"replication.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 220, \\\"end_line\\\": 300, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" },\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"src-repl-snap11\\\", \\\"file\\\": \\\"replication.go\\\", \\\"start_line\\\": 299, \\\"end_line\\\": 375, \\\"kind\\\": \\\"code_observation\\\" }\n  ],\n  \\\"investigations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"ref\\\": \\\"@q-compaction-cause\\\",\n      \\\"question\\\": \\\"Is the snapshot-boundary loop caused specifically by the leader's compaction leaving its retained log above the index the follower's prev-log check needs, so that the identical history converges when the leader keeps a few trailing entries?\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-compact11\\\", \\\"src-repl11\\\", \\\"src-repl-snap11\\\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"interpretations\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"@q-compaction-cause\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-compact11\\\", \\\"src-repl11\\\", \\\"src-repl-snap11\\\"],\n      \\\"conclusion\\\": \\\"unresolved\\\",\n      \\\"defect_claim\\\": \\\"unresolved\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Construction feedback from the sealed-partition harness, run locally with both settings and otherwise identical inputs, separates the cause. TrailingLogs=0: divergent_prefix reports base_index 2, divergence_index 3, partitioned_leader_last_index 7, partner_last_index 7, partner_store 1..7; successor_snapshot reports snapshot_index 4 with successor_store 0/0; rejoin_observe reports restores_before 0, restores_early 724, restores_late 734, partner_applied_index 4 pinned at the snapshot index and partner_last_index 7. TrailingLogs=3: the precondition is identical (partner_store 1..7 with earlier-term entries from index 3), the successor's snapshot is at the same index 4 but its store now retains 2..4, and rejoin_observe reports restores_before/early/late all 0 with partner_applied_index 4 and partner_last_index 4 - the follower's stale suffix was replaced by ordinary AppendEntries and no snapshot was needed. So the loop's necessary condition is the leader's retained log starting above the index needed to rebuild the request (which is what sends replicateTo to SEND_SNAP); retaining even a few entries below the boundary lets the leader back the prev-log index down into entries it still holds, and the follower truncates its stale suffix normally. This is recorded as construction feedback only: no measured conclusion is asserted in this batch, and the earlier retained witness (CheckRun f66fa4e4e0514f7e95b7788032144a30, TrailingLogs=0) and the assertion built on it stand on their own basis.\\\",\n      \\\"counterevidence\\\": [\n        \\\"With TrailingLogs=3 the same history converges with zero snapshot installs, so leader compaction past the boundary is load-bearing and the loop is not a property of the partition, the uncommitted suffix or the snapshot itself.\\\",\n        \\\"The default TrailingLogs (10240) would delay but not remove the condition: it is reached once the leader's log extends that far past its snapshot index, which this harness did not sample.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"limitations\\\": [\n        \\\"Source-only in this batch: the two-case harness has not been executed by the controller yet, so the quoted counts are non-retained local runs.\\\",\n        \\\"Only trailing values 0 and 3 were compared, at one snapshot index and one configuration; the exact threshold (how many trailing entries suffice) was not characterised.\\\",\n        \\\"The harness counts InstallSnapshot installs via the follower FSM's Restore count rather than on the wire, and no RPC-level trace is collected.\\\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"experiment\\\": {\n    \\\"investigation_id\\\": \\\"@q-compaction-cause\\\",\n    \\\"previous_id\\\": \\\"b836c3a8cfc549188ebed6183f15f019-experiment\\\",\n    \\\"revision_reason\\\": \\\"Same sealed-partition scenario, now executed twice in one harness with TrailingLogs=0 and TrailingLogs=3 so the compaction depth is the only difference between the cases; each emitted event carries trailing_logs to keep the two runs apart. No other scenario change.\\\",\n    \\\"harness_path\\\": \\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n    \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"src-compact11\\\", \\\"src-repl11\\\", \\\"src-repl-snap11\\\"],\n    \\\"scope\\\": {\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Five-node legal history per case: {leader, partner} isolated from the other three in both directions, the leader replicating uncommitted commands to the partner only, a successor elected by the majority that commits its entry at the first divergent index and snapshots there under the case's TrailingLogs, then a heal. Observations: the precondition, the successor's snapshot and store bounds, per-node timeline, and the partner's InstallSnapshot count over ~1.5 s.\\\",\n      \\\"assumptions\\\": [\n        \\\"Both cases share the rest of the configuration, so any difference in the partner's outcome is attributable to how much log the successor retains.\\\",\n        \\\"Sealing the partition on both sides is required for the partner to be genuinely isolated, as established by the superseded harness.\\\",\n        \\\"The partner's FSM Restore count identifies InstallSnapshot installs without touching production logic.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"excluded\\\": [\n        \\\"No RPC-level instrumentation, no network transport, and no default (10240) TrailingLogs sampling.\\\",\n        \\\"The threshold at which the loop disappears is not characterised.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"parameters\\\": { \\\"peers\\\": 5, \\\"trailing_logs_cases\\\": [0, 3], \\\"uncommitted_commands\\\": 5, \\\"observation_window_ms\\\": 1500 }\n    },\n    \\\"prefix\\\": \\\"For trailing in {0,3}: MakeClusterCustom(Peers=5, Bootstrap=true, Conf{TrailingLogs: trailing, SnapshotInterval:1h, SnapshotThreshold:1<<20, HeartbeatTimeout/ElectionTimeout/LeaderLeaseTimeout:1s, CommitTimeout:10ms}, MakeFSMFunc returning a Restore-counting MockFSM). Wait for a leader; partner=followers[0], others=remaining three; disconnect leader<->other and partner<->other in both directions and emit partition; base=leader.LastIndex(); fire five leader.Apply calls; wait until partner.LastIndex()>base and emit divergent_prefix with trailing_logs; wait up to 12 s for a successor among others, apply one command, Snapshot(), emit successor_snapshot with its store bounds; FullyConnect(); emit a per-node timeline at 0/200/400/700/1000/1300 ms with states, indexes, store bounds, entry terms at 3/4/5 and the partner's Restore count; finally emit rejoin_observe with the restore counts, the partner's and successor's indexes and store bounds, and trailing_logs.\\\",\n    \\\"responsibility\\\": \\\"The audit must identify which mechanism carries the failure: compaction depth, partition, or the snapshot transfer itself.\\\"\n  }\n}\nJSON\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update-11.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
